/-!
# Chapter 19: Hyperfinite Approximation

Complete formalization of Robert Goldblatt's *Lectures on the Hyperreals: An Introduction to
Nonstandard Analysis* (GTM 188, Springer, 1998), Chapter 19 (pp. 259–278):

* **Chapter 19 Introduction — The Hyperfinite Approximation Methodology** (p. 259):
  - Fine ultrafilter `fineUltrafilter α := Ultrafilter.of (Filter.atTop : Filter (Finset α))` on
    finite subsets `Finset α`, ultrapower `StarElem α`, standard embedding `stdElem`, internal
    subsets `internalApproxSet`, hyperfinite subsets `IsHyperfiniteApproxSet`, and the canonical
    hyperfinite approximant `canonicalHyperfiniteApprox α` satisfying `A ⊆ B ⊆ *A`.

* **§19.1 Colourings and Graphs — De Bruijn–Erdős Theorem** (pp. 260–261):
  - Partition-based `r`-colourings of sets (`IsSetPartitionColoring`) and graphs (`ColourFormula`,
    **Exercise 19.1.1**), restriction to subsets/subgraphs, enlargement transfer, and equivalence
    with `SimpleGraph.Colorable`.
  - Enlarged graph `starGraph G` on `StarElem V` preserving adjacency on standard vertices.
  - **De Bruijn–Erdős `k`-Colouring Theorem** (`deBruijn_erdos_colorable_iff` and
    `deBruijn_erdos_rel_iff`): proved via hyperfinite approximation on `canonicalHyperfiniteApprox V`
    and finiteness of `Fin k`, plus chromatic number corollary `chromaticNumber_eq_iSup_finset`.

* **§19.2–19.3 Boolean Algebras, Formula Algebras `B_Π`, and Atomic Finite Algebras** (pp. 262–267):
  - Propositional `Π`-formulae (`PropFormula`), valuations, tautologies, inconsistency, and the
    Lindenbaum–Tarski Boolean algebra `FormulaAlgebra Π` (`B_Π`).
  - **Exercise 19.2.1**: disjunctive normal form realization of every set of valuations when `Π` is
    finite, Boolean isomorphism with `(Π → Bool) → Bool`, and exact cardinality `|B_Π| = 2^(2^n)`.
  - Atomlessness of `FormulaAlgebra Π` when `Π` is infinite (`formulaAlgebra_no_atoms_of_infinite`).
  - Atoms (`Atoms B`), atom laws below `⊓`, `⊔`, `ᶜ`, homomorphism `atomsBelowHom : B → 𝒫(Atoms B)`,
    representation of atomic Boolean algebras as fields of sets, and **Finite Boolean Algebra
    Representation** (`finiteBooleanAlgebra_orderIso_powerset_atoms`: every finite Boolean algebra
    is atomic and isomorphic to `Set (Atoms B)` with `|B| = 2^|Atoms B|`).

* **§19.4–19.7 Hyperfinite Approximating Algebras, Stone's Representation Theorem, Ultrafilter
  Theorem, and Distributive Lattices** (pp. 267–273):
  - Local finiteness of Boolean algebras (`closure_finset_finite` and cardinality bound `≤ 2^(2^n)`
    both via minterms and via **Exercise 19.5(2)** quotient from `FormulaAlgebra (Fin n)`).
  - Hyperfinite atomic Boolean subalgebra `hyperfiniteApproxSubalgebra B` (`B⁺`) between `B` and
    `*B`, **Exercise 19.5(1)** (smallest internal subalgebra generated by a hyperfinite subset is
    hyperfinite), and immediate hyperfinite proof that every Boolean algebra embeds into a power set
    algebra (`stoneHyperfiniteRep`).
  - Boolean filters (`BoolFilter B`), ultrafilters (`BoolUltrafilter B`), 2-valued homomorphisms,
    **Exercise 19.7(1)** (ultrafilter induced by an atom of `B⁺`), **Exercise 19.7(2)** (every
    internal filter of `B⁺` is principal), and Goldblatt's nonstandard hyperfinite-approximation
    proof of the **Boolean Ultrafilter Theorem** (`exists_boolUltrafilter_extending`).
  - **Stone's Representation Theorem**: injective Boolean embedding into `Set (BoolUltrafilter B)`
    AND full topological **Stone Duality** (`stoneClopenIso`: isomorphism of `B` with the Boolean
    algebra `TopologicalSpace.Clopens (StoneSpace B)` of clopen sets of its compact totally
    disconnected Hausdorff Stone space).
  - **Exercise 19.7(3)** (monadic element in `*I` belonging to every member of a nonprincipal
    ultrafilter on `I`) and **Exercise 19.7(4)(a)–(b)** (distributive lattice representation as a
    set lattice and prime filter extension via join-irreducible elements and hyperfinite
    approximation).

* **§19.8–19.11 Hyperfinite-Dimensional Vector Spaces & Hahn–Banach Theorem** (pp. 273–278):
  - Hyperreal vector spaces `*E_𝒰`, hyperfinite vector sums (`hyperVecSum`), **Exercise 19.8.1**,
    **Theorem 19.8.2** (hyperfinite-dimensional subspace `V⁺` containing `E`), and
    **Exercises 19.9(1)–(3)** (hyperfinite span, transcendence of `r ∈ ℝ* \ ℝ` over `ℝ`, linear
    independence of `{r^n}`, and infinite-dimensionality of `ℝ*` and `𝕃` over `ℝ`).
  - Sublinear functionals (`IsPosHomogeneous`, `IsSubadditive`, `IsSublinear`), one-step extension
    (**Lemma 19.10.1**, `hahn_banach_one_step`), and finite-dimensional extension
    (`hahn_banach_finset`).
  - Generic ultrapower limited numbers `LimitedGermSubmodule U` and shadow functional
    `shadowGermLinearMap U` (**Exercise 19.11(1)**), hyperlinear functional `f⁺` (**Exercise
    19.11(2)**), **Goldblatt's Nonstandard Proof of the Full Hahn–Banach Theorem**
    (`hahn_banach_extension`), **Exercise 19.11(3)** (Luxemburg's direct ultrapower proof), and
    normed-space corollaries (`hahn_banach_symmetric`, `hahn_banach_norm_preserving`,
    `exists_dual_vector_norm`, `separating_dual_of_ne`).
-/

noncomputable section

namespace Goldblatt.Ch19

open Filter Set
